2. AI models and weights — not covered by part 1
------------------------------------------------

No model weights are included in this package. The application downloads them
from Hugging Face into config/models on first use, and they remain under their own
licences, as does audio generated with them.

**stabilityai/stable-audio-open-1.0**
Licence: Stability AI Community License (Hugging Face licence name
`stable-audio-community`). Free for research, non-commercial and limited
commercial use; commercial use above the revenue threshold stated in the
agreement requires a paid licence from Stability AI, and commercial use
requires registration. Read the full text before commercial use:
  https://huggingface.co/stabilityai/stable-audio-open-1.0/blob/main/LICENSE.md
  https://stability.ai/community-license
  https://stability.ai/license

Audio you generate with these models is yours to use within the terms of the
model licence that produced it; this application claims no rights over it and
cannot grant rights the model licence withholds.

**stabilityai/stable-audio-3-small-music**
**stabilityai/stable-audio-3-small-sfx**
**stabilityai/stable-audio-3-medium**
Licence: Stability AI Community License (Hugging Face licence name
`stable-audio-community`) — the same family of terms as Stable Audio Open 1.0,
accepted per repository. The bundled T5Gemma text encoder is additionally
redistributed under the Gemma Terms of Use (<https://ai.google.dev/gemma/terms>),
including its use restrictions. All
three repositories are gated: the files are only served to accounts that have
accepted the terms while signed in. Check the licence on the repository page
before publishing or monetising generated audio.

All Stable Audio names and marks belong to Stability AI Ltd. This application is
an independent client for those models and is not affiliated with, endorsed by
or supported by Stability AI.


3. Third-party software — installed, not bundled
------------------------------------------------

run.bat / run.sh install these into ./.venv (from PyPI, the PyTorch wheel index
or the stable-audio-3 GitHub archive); their licences and the notices they ship
with apply unchanged, and transitive dependencies keep their own licences:

  PyTorch, torchaudio                 BSD-3-Clause
  diffusers, transformers             Apache-2.0
  accelerate, huggingface_hub         Apache-2.0
  safetensors, torchsde               Apache-2.0
  einops, einops-exts                 MIT
  numpy, soundfile                    BSD-3-Clause
  PySide6 / Qt for Python             LGPL-3.0 (Qt itself: LGPL-3.0 / GPL / commercial)
  lameenc                             LGPL-3.0-or-later (bundled LAME:
                                      LGPL-2.0-or-later); MP3 patents expired 2017
  stable_audio_3 (source archive)     MIT (Stability AI)

`run.bat` / `run.sh` also download a portable CPython build
(python-build-standalone) into `./.python` when no suitable interpreter is
found; that runtime is Python itself, under the PSF licence, and its build
scripts are MPL-2.0. Neither is bundled with this package.

**PySide6 note.** The GUI uses PySide6, the official Qt for Python binding, which
is LGPL-3.0. That allows this application to be distributed as closed source or
commercially, provided you keep Qt dynamically linked (the wheel does), ship the
LGPL-3.0 text, keep the Qt copyright notices intact, and let users replace the Qt
libraries with their own build. Static linking or modifying Qt itself would bring
the GPL-3.0 obligations back. The earlier PyQt6 dependency was removed for exactly
this reason: PyQt6 is GPL-3.0 unless a commercial Riverbank licence is bought.


4. Changing this licence
------------------------

The application code is the author's to license. To use a different licence for
part 1, replace the text of section 1 (keeping sections 2 and 3, which describe
third-party terms you cannot relicense), bump APP_VERSION in code/app.py and rebuild
the delivery with _dev/build_delivery.py.
